WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.135
Turning now to tragedy this evening

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.303
at a Florida hospital.

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.337
A 76 year

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.139
old woman is in custody

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.441
after allegedly shooting and killing

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.877
her terminally ill husband.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:13.146
She then apparently barricaded herself

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.581
in his hospital room,

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.482
forcing officials

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.282
to evacuate

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.484
staff and patients

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:19.519
and declare a lockdown.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.621
No one else was threatened or injured.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:22.288
Daytona Beach

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.157
police said an investigation determined

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.259
the couple planned this weeks ago.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.930
Apparently because he was terminally ill.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.600
They had a conversation about it

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.235
and they actually planned this

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.903
approximately three weeks ago,

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.705
that if he continued to take a turn

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.907
for the worse that she wanted,

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:42.942
he wanted her to end this.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:43.610
Initially,

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.979
I think the plan was a murder suicide.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:47.680
So she killed him

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.415
and then she was going

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:50.116
to turn the gun on herself,

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.051
but decided she

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.285
couldn't go through with it.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.120
And we

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:54.754
were told the woman's

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.856
husband was 77 years old.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.725
She could be facing a first degree

00:00:58.725 --> 00:00:59.993
murder charge.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.161
CNN national security

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:02.962
analyst Juliette Kayyem joins us.

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:03.263
Juliette,

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.432
this is such a sad story

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:07.300
for so many reasons, right

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.069
Have you ever heard of a murder suicide

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.703
inside a hospital?

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:11.204
Obviously,

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:11.871
she didn't follow

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:12.872
through on the suicide part.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.307
That was part of the plan.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:14.574
I mean,

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.742
would it be relatively easy

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:16.543
at most hospitals

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:19.212
to get a gun into someone's room?

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:19.679
Yes.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:22.248
And I mean, part of this is not.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:22.715
No matter

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.684
how strong security measures are

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.686
and they're certainly worth looking at

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.522
you can't sort of sort of plan

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.658
for every scenario, including this one,

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:32.826
which is just you know,

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.794
it's just tragic any way you look at it.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.596
I'm not defending any of the decisions

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:37.664
this couple

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:40.366
decides that they want to go together,

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.000
so to speak,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.002
and she can't follow through and

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.772
and barricades herself.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.707
The challenge at a hospital is family

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:49.042
members are treated

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.844
as sort of trusted visitors

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:53.012
as they should be, especially if ever.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.914
If a spouse is terminally ill,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.449
spouses will come in and out

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.818
that a lot of them will get badged.

00:01:58.818 --> 00:01:59.853
Any parent

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:00.653
listening knows that

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.222
when your children come visit it

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.223
or have to be in hospitals,

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:04.858
that's the same thing.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:08.161
And so there are sort of their insiders.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.064
And so you're sort of not expecting this

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:11.731
at this stage.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.432
My assumption

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:14.067
is that they don't have metal detectors,

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:14.400
at least

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.269
that all the doors at the hospital

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:17.737
they may want to check in to this,

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.405
but this is rare murder-suicide.

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:23.943
I tend to be either quite violent, right?

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:24.811
A man

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.813
killing his wife and then himself

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.882
or tend to be quite private.

00:02:28.882 --> 00:02:30.617
And this is this is just unique

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:35.622
and hopefully, you know, as that the wife

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.658
charging her with first degree murder

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:39.759
will probably be taken

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.528
into account in terms of,

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:42.061
of course,

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.997
the circumstances of the decision

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.999
that that couple made. Right.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:48.735
The agreement that police said that

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:49.736
the husband had asked her,

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.037
according to police, to kill him

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.238
if his condition got worse,

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.673
he was terminally ill.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:54.541
How do police

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:56.242
deal with this type of situation?

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:56.342
I mean,

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:56.843
they were able

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:59.913
to get the woman to surrender.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.514
So at some stage when they know

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:02.916
it's not a true active shooter,

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:03.816
like the kinds that you and

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:04.317
I think

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:04.951
about her off

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.586
and on about in terms of someone

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:08.454
just basically wants the body count.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:08.755
Right.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:09.722
That this is

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:12.358
this is a situation in which it was quite

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:15.428
planned and and targeted.

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:16.563
And their only concern is

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.298
if there were other patients

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:19.432
in that room which

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:20.533
which it appears that there weren't

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:20.800
and then,

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.936
of course, the patients that are around

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:24.871
that room and protecting them.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.072
So they're going to treat this

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:28.741
and did treat this as a as a more typical

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.143
rather than active shooter.

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.377
As a hostage situation.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.545
There was no reason to believe

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:34.380
she was after anyone else.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.115
They probably likely knew her

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.483
because he had been in the hospital

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.352
at least a couple of weeks.

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:42.088
And so they're able to bring her out

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:44.123
without further harm to herself

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:48.061
and then to get the care that she needs.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:48.261
You know,

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:50.630
we sometimes think of these cases,

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:50.863
you know,

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.732
in the sort of safety security lens

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.300
and why how could this happen?

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.569
And sometimes there are situations

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:56.903
in which

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:57.203
you really

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:59.239
can't sort of plan for

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.975
because they're so unique and maybe

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:03.943
just just different and kind,

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.678
which this one is

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:06.846
and one in which

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:08.081
I think the authorities are

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:10.049
are really going to have to think about

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.951
whether first degree murder is

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.953
is the appropriate charge

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:15.955
given the circumstances

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:17.457
and context that we know.

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:18.925
Joining us now is Dr.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.426
Joshua Hornstein.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.394
He's a cardiologist

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:22.795
who had a shelter in place

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.731
at ADVENTHEALTH Hospital in Daytona Beach

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:26.899
while all of this was unfolding.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:27.233
Dr.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:29.235
Hornstein, thank you for being with us.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:29.702
No doubt

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.471
this had to be a frightening moment

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.972
for you other staffers.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.440
Can you walk us through what happened?

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:36.042
Certainly.

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:37.410
Thanks for having me.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.411
First, I just have to say

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:39.312
how appreciative

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.247
I am of all the law enforcement

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:43.283
who were there, how quickly they acted

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:44.550
and how they were able

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.952
to resolve the situation

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:48.488
about their loss of life.

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:48.988
Well,

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.356
it it was

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:51.157
it was pretty scary,

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:53.059
especially in the early part of it.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:55.261
We just had no idea what was going on.

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:58.097
I was around in the emergency department

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:00.099
when a

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.000
announcement came

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.503
by the overhead speakers saying

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:07.507
yellow and we get colds all the time.

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:08.641
That referred to,

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:09.609
you know, patients

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:11.611
having cardiac distress.

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.912
But yellow is not something

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:14.080
you need to have ever heard before.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.548
So people are looking on their badges

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:17.250
to see what that even means.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.952
And it says lockdown so well, again,

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:20.553
looking at each other

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:22.755
like lockdown to do about that.

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:24.824
And then another 10 seconds later,

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.259
another alarm goes off

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:28.961
saying cold shoulder shelter in place.

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:31.998
And that's where pandemonium started.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:33.966
But in a controlled pandemonium,

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:35.168
everyone started

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:36.536
getting all the patients

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:38.338
behind their closed doors

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:39.772
and a nurse

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.974
who had to get into the supply closet.

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.343
So she and I went in there

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:46.479
and we basically just sat there

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.514
for the next 30, 40 minutes

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:49.582
until we started

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:50.717
getting some information

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:53.720
out to Twitter about what was going on.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.087
Dr..

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:55.321
Yeah, we were just showing the video

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:56.022
a few moments ago.

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:58.124
We showed again of the video

00:05:58.124 --> 00:06:01.294
I think you took inside that supply room.

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:02.762
Yes.

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:03.363
I mean,

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.797
what was going through your mind

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:06.699
when you were waiting in there?

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:09.068
So for the first few seconds,

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:11.938
like this is just like any other fire.

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:13.706
All been through my whole life.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.742
It's not it's not real.

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:17.810
But there were a couple of moments

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:18.911
when you would hear

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:20.913
door slamming and raised voices,

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:24.283
and it's hard not to flash back any video

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:25.651
of any mass shooting at all

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.487
seen over these years.

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:28.955
And suddenly it is real.

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:31.724
And you don't know that it's an old lady

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:32.625
on the top floor.

00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:34.160
You just thought, you know,

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.628
there's a shooter outside the room.

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:36.896
If you saw the picture of the

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:40.533
stretcher barricading the door

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:41.467
and, you know,

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.602
you're looking at that saying

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:44.170
is only going to stop the shooter

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.705
if they want to get in here?

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:47.507
That's what's going through your mind.

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:48.541
Yeah. And Dr.

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:51.210
I mean, your reaction to the fact

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.278
that somebody was able to

00:06:52.278 --> 00:06:53.980
I mean, obviously,

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.448
this was a tragic situation

00:06:55.448 --> 00:06:57.183
where this woman

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:58.284
and her husband apparently

00:06:58.284 --> 00:06:59.152
took it upon themselves

00:06:59.152 --> 00:07:00.319
to do this sort of thing.

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:02.588
But your reaction to somebody

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:04.257
being able to bring a gun into a hospital

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:05.191
like that?

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:06.259
It's terrible.

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:06.492
You know,

00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:07.593
this isn't even the first time

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:08.161
in my career

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:08.928
this has happened

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:10.830
when I was in training in San Diego,

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.098
murder suicide

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:14.600
almost exactly like this of patients

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.369
who were a patient

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:18.070
who was terminally ill.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.338
And, you know, it

00:07:19.338 --> 00:07:20.940
speaks a lot for gun

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.041
violence in the country.

00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:23.843
Even though they had this pact.

00:07:23.843 --> 00:07:25.878
Is this going the way to do it?

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:26.879
It was so violent

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:30.016
and and and so distress and distress,

00:07:30.016 --> 00:07:30.650
sort of not

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:31.484
not just the staff,

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:33.219
but all the patients that are there

00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:34.554
trying to recover and healing

00:07:34.554 --> 00:07:36.789
what's going on. I mean, it was dreadful.

00:07:37.824 --> 00:07:39.192
And did you talk to other

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:40.159
folks there

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:42.895
